SPU: resident code ownership on every lookup, verified streamed regions, per-thread dispatch cache (open upstream PR
#481, stacked on #420 and #419, imported as is).

Resistance 3's job dispatcher loads each Insomniac job module at LS 0x100, over the policy module (igPm, 0xA00) that
started it. The interpreter's rejoin probe (spu_lifted_lookup) looked up the context's own image inside such a resident
span and ran igPm's stale lift over the job's bytes: the job's first call into 0xA00 ran igPm again, which went back to
waiting for a signal, and the job never completed. #419 makes the rejoin probe and spu_indirect_branch resolve through
the resident regions first; #420 adds verified regions; #481 caches the lookup per thread (SPU_DISPATCH_CACHE=0 turns
it off). This replaces most of our spu-runtime/0001, which keeps the drain-resume path the PRs do not touch.
spu_context changes: the module must be rebuilt.

Test: runtime/spu/tests/test_spu_lifted_start.c and the PR's other tests; scripted run to gameplay (jobs complete).

Upstream: PR #481 (with #419, #420; drop this file when the pin contains them).

